course: dictionary
lesson: 273
title: Ambulance
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An ambulance is a special vehicle with trained people and medical equipment. It takes sick or injured people to hospital quickly. The word can also mean the service itself, as in «call an ambulance».
explain: In an emergency, call the emergency number for where you live. Say the word «ambulance», give the address, and stay on the line until help arrives.
explain: Use the words around a new word to understand it. «Paramedics are the trained helpers who come in an ambulance.» The sentence tells you that paramedics are the trained people inside the ambulance.
fact: An ambulance is a special vehicle that takes sick or injured people to hospital quickly.
fact: Paramedics are the trained helpers who travel in an ambulance.
fact: Emergency numbers differ by country: 911 in the USA and Canada, 999 or 112 in the UK and Ireland, 000 in Australia, 111 in New Zealand.
fact: When an ambulance comes with lights and sirens, cars pull over to let it pass.
fact: «Ambulance» can mean the vehicle or the service, as in «call an ambulance».
exercise: «Paramedics are the trained helpers who come in an ambulance.» Who are the paramedics? | *Trained helpers who come in an ambulance | People who sell tickets at the hospital | Children who ride in the back | Drivers of buses to school
exercise: Which number do you call for an emergency in Australia? | 111 | 999 | 911 | *000
exercise: «Cars pull over when an ambulance comes with lights and sirens.» Why do cars pull over? | To race it to the hospital | To follow it home | *To let the ambulance pass | To park and have lunch
test: In an emergency in the UK, you can call 999 or which other number? | 111 | *112 | 000 | 911
test: What does «air ambulance» most likely mean? | A van that sells ice cream | A bus with no windows | *A special ambulance that travels through the air | A balloon shaped like a van
exam: When you call for help in an emergency, what should you do? | Hang up quickly and wait | Send a text with a photo | *Say «ambulance», give the address and stay on the line | Hide under the table
